  "notes": "TCL 85RM7L Google TV (device G08, model \"Smart TV Pro\", MediaTek tcl9618 / mt5896)\nAndroid 14 (Google TV), firmware UTT2.250416.001 AU02, product G08_4K_GB, security patch 2025-12-05.\nAbout 2.4 GB RAM. Same board and firmware build as examples/tcl-c755-google-tv; that list was the\nstarting point. Debloat only: the stock Google TV launcher stays, so setupwraith stays too.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/tcl-85rm7l-google-tv/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/tcl-85rm7l-google-tv/debloat.txt com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx\nTV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/venv/bin/python -I tools/tv.py 'settings delete secure screensaver_components'\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nKept on purpose: Chromecast (com.google.android.apps.mediashell), AirPlay (com.tcl.airplay2,\ncom.mediatek.AirplayAPK, com.mediatek.airplaydaemon), Miracast (com.tcl.miracast), the game bar,\nthe USB media player and gallery, Google Assistant (katniss) and com.google.android.tv.remote.service\n(it carries the remote's mic button), plus everything the C755 header lists as Keep.\nFirmware updates come from Google Play Services (SYSTEM_UPDATE_SETTINGS resolves to\ncom.google.android.gms/.update.SystemUpdatePanoActivity), so disabling com.tcl.ttvs leaves them alone.\n\nTested 2026-10-20 on a real unit, applied in five batches with screenshots between them: Home, YouTube,\nLive TV (com.tcl.tv/com.tcl.player.TVActivity), the Input key's source panel (com.tcl.suspension, AirPlay\nand TV tiles), the four HDMI inputs in tv_input, Chromecast advertised over mDNS, and the AirPlay,\nMiracast and Assistant processes all kept working, and all 22 packages stayed disabled after a reboot.\nA USB DAC powered from the TV's USB port kept its power with USB debugging on.\nThe source panel's Apps row keeps showing TCL Channel and User Guide tiles, which no longer open.\n\nKnown trade-off: com.tcl.ttvs is one package holding Samba TV ACR, TCL BI analytics, Alexa core AND\nthe T-Cast server (TVSServerService, CastService). Disabling it stops T-Cast; com.tcl.magiconnectfree\nis left enabled but has nothing to talk to.\nTCL tracking and analytics",
